# Tests ycxx is expected to fail with the features it has (tests/features/ycxx.txt): one
# `<test id> <reason>` per line, the reason being ycxx's first diagnostic. Most need what the α
# subset lacks (classes, templates, the preprocessor's directives). An XPASS fails the run, so a
# line goes when ycxx starts passing its test (tests/driver/toolchain.py: ycxx_xfails).
